  "evidence": {
    "compilation": [],
    "runtime": "Pending Hardware Verification",
    "expectedObservations": [
      "Memcheck should identify the defect executable's single global-memory out-of-bounds write, while the corrected executable should preserve the 32 intended writes without that bounds defect.",
      "Racecheck should identify the defect executable's plain shared-memory read-after-write ordering hazard, while the corrected executable should preserve the produced value with a block barrier.",
      "Initcheck should identify the defect executable's read from uninitialized device global memory, while the corrected executable should preserve the increment work after zero-initializing the input.",
      "Synccheck should identify the defect executable's divergent conditional __syncthreads, while the corrected executable should preserve the phase copy with uniform block participation."
    ],
